From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:44:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/37] Read asset catalogs with Iris's host

UIKit on Linux (Iris's OpenUIKit) reads the same asset catalogs for
UIImage(named:), so the reader and the encoded image it gives move to the
IrisHost target in Iris's runtimes/ios, next to the window's scene.
OpenSwiftUICore keeps turning an image set's template rendering intent
into its own rendering mode.
---
 .../View/Image/GraphicsImage.swift            |  20 +--
 .../View/Image/IrisAssetCatalog.swift         | 164 ------------------
 .../View/Image/NamedImage.swift               |   5 +-
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 180 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 Sources/OpenSwiftUICore/View/Image/IrisAssetCatalog.swift

